            {
              "t": "h",
              "text": "Wikinaut"
            },
            {
              "t": "p",
              "text": "A space-themed navigation game for Wikipedia. Name a destination article and your ship flies the shortest link path there, hop by hop, through the real links on each live page."
            },
            {
              "t": "plate",
              "art": "starmap"
            },
            {
              "t": "note",
              "text": "Python · Flask · JavaScript · SQLite · Fly.io"
            },
            {
              "t": "credit",
              "text": "The backend is a fork of Six Degrees of Wikipedia (jwngr/sdow) by Jacob Wenger."
            },
            {
              "t": "actions",
              "items": [
                {
                  "label": "Open project",
                  "href": "https://github.com/jackcareynapa/wikinaut#install-the-userscript",
                  "kind": "primary"
                },
                {
                  "label": "View source",
                  "href": "https://github.com/jackcareynapa/wikinaut",
                  "kind": "secondary"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "t": "kicker",
              "text": "How to play"
            },
            {
              "t": "steps",
              "items": [
                {
                  "title": "Set coordinates",
                  "text": "Open any English Wikipedia article and type a destination into the console. Autocomplete helps."
                },
                {
                  "title": "Chart course",
                  "text": "The backend finds the shortest link path and draws it as a star map. When several routes tie, the pager steps through them."
                },
                {
                  "title": "Launch",
                  "text": "The ship flies to each next link on the page and jumps through hyperspace to the next article, until you arrive."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "t": "kicker",
              "text": "How it works"
            },
            {
              "t": "diagram",
              "nodes": [
                {
                  "label": "Userscript",
                  "sub": "console + flight on the live page"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Flask API",
                  "sub": "Docker on Fly.io"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Bidirectional BFS",
                  "sub": "memory-mapped CSR arrays"
                },
                {
                  "label": "SQLite link graph",
                  "sub": "built from Wikipedia dumps"
                }
              ],
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "t": "list",
              "items": [
                "Rebuilt the multi-GB data pipeline in Python 3 for Wikipedia's 2024 schema change, which silently broke upstream builds.",
                "Live-page link matching handles redirects, two page renderers and collapsed sections, with a direct-URL fallback."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
